---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import DocCard from '../../../components/DocCard.astro';
const sidebar = [
  { title: 'Documentation Home', href: '/docs' },
  { title: 'Observability Overview', href: '/docs/observability' },
  { title: 'SIEM & Log Pipeline', href: '/docs/observability/siem' },
  { title: 'Kibana Dashboards', href: '/docs/observability/kibana', active: true },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'registry', text: 'Dashboard Registry', level: 2 },
  { id: 'timeline', text: 'Pattern Report Timeline', level: 2 },
  { id: 'modules', text: 'Python Module Reference', level: 2 },
  { id: 'honest', text: 'Honest Assessment', level: 2 },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Kibana Dashboards" description="Visual dashboards for monitoring honeypot activity" section="Observability" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <p>
    Seven saved dashboards cover alert triage, aggregate threat posture, decisioning, session behaviour,
    attack patterns and threat intelligence. All of them are generated from Python and committed as NDJSON,
    so the same definition can be rebuilt offline or imported into a live Kibana.
  </p>
  <CardGrid columns={3}>
    <DocCard title="6 registered views" icon="chart" tag="Operational" description="Alerts, web threat overview, decisions and decay, session analysis, attack patterns and threat intelligence." meta="dashboard-* IDs" />
    <DocCard title="Timeline capture" icon="eye" tag="Evidence" description="A dedicated embed-mode dashboard renders a pattern's request timeline before a screenshot is taken." meta="per-pattern" />
    <DocCard title="Review friendly" icon="branch" tag="Code-managed" description="Layouts live in Python, so changes are reviewable and exportable rather than click-only state." meta="NDJSON in git" />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2 id="registry">Dashboard Registry</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Dashboard ID</th><th>Title</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-ids-alerts</td><td>Honeypot: IDS Alerts (Suricata)</td><td>Real-time IDS alert triage</td></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-web-threat-overview</td><td>Honeypot: Web Traffic & Threat Overview</td><td>Aggregate web threat posture</td></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-threat-decisions</td><td>Honeypot: Threat Decisions & Decay</td><td>Decisioning logic and threat decay</td></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-session-analysis</td><td>Honeypot: Session Analysis</td><td>Session-level attacker behavior</td></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-attack-patterns</td><td>Honeypot: Attack Patterns</td><td>Pattern-based attack analysis</td></tr>
    <tr><td>dashboard-threat-intel</td><td>Honeypot: Threat Intelligence</td><td>Threat intelligence integrations</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>Each dashboard is built via <code>_dashboard(dash_id, title, description, layout)</code> and registered as <code>("dashboard", did, body)</code> objects in <code>saved_objects/honeypot-dashboards.ndjson</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="timeline">Pattern Report Timeline Dashboard</h2>
  <p>A dedicated pattern report timeline dashboard (<code>pattern-report-request-timeline-dashboard</code>) is used in embed mode to capture screenshots of request timelines for specific patterns.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Automates a login process (via autologin script if configured) to access Kibana.</li>
    <li>Imports the necessary saved objects using the Kibana API.</li>
    <li>Loads the specific timeline dashboard in <strong>embed mode</strong> for a given time window.</li>
    <li>Waits for a rendering signal (checking for a "render complete" flag) before capturing a screenshot.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="modules">Dashboard Python Module Reference</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Module</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Key Functions</th></tr>
    <tr><td>build_dashboards.py</td><td>Generates dashboard objects and visualizations into NDJSON</td><td>_dashboard(), dashboard registration</td></tr>
    <tr><td>export_dashboards.py</td><td>Exports live dashboard objects from Kibana to local NDJSON</td><td>Export by dashboard ID list</td></tr>
    <tr><td>kibana_timeline.py</td><td>Defines structure and payload for request timeline visualization</td><td>DASHBOARD_ID, _dashboard_body(), NDJSON generation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>kibana_timeline_capture.py</td><td>Client-side workflow for live dashboard capture</td><td>Autologin, Kibana API import, embed-mode loading, screenshot capture</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2 id="honest">Honest Assessment</h2>
  <p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Offline generation is idempotent. Export workflow preserves manual panel edits. Timeline capture enables per-pattern visual evidence.</p>
  <p><strong>Limitations:</strong> Dashboard generation and export are separate scripts with potential drift. Timeline capture depends on Kibana auth setup. Layout defined in Python code (not editable JSON). No automated dashboard health monitoring.</p>
</DocsLayout>
